// The `flock-selector` layout: the project picker as the whole session. This is
// what bare `flock` and `flock pick` open, and it is reachable directly with
// `flock --layout flock-selector`.
//
// The picker is the session's only pane, deliberately. It used to float over a
// shell, which needed `tail -f /dev/null` underneath it as a keepalive — an
// interactive shell can exit during its own startup and tear the session down
// before the WASM plugin has finished loading. A plugin pane cannot exit, so
// making the picker the base pane removes both the race and the sacrificial
// process. There is also nothing useful to put underneath: this session exists
// only to choose what to work on.
//
// This layout deliberately carries no folder args. The picker resolves them from
// the `flock` section of config.kdl, which is the one place they are stated:
// setting `root_dirs` there reaches this layout, the `Super s` keybinding, and
// the sidebar in every project session alike. Restating them here would not just
// be redundant — a set that disagreed with the keybinding's would make `Super s`
// miss the running picker and launch a second one.
layout {
    pane borderless=true {
        plugin location="flock-selector" {
            // Name this entry session so it is always the same one (and the
            // sidebar hides it) instead of a random throwaway name accumulating
            // in the workspace list. Bare `flock` already creates the session
            // under this name, which makes the rename a no-op; it still matters
            // when this layout is opened by hand with `--layout`.
            //
            // Must match `FLOCK_SELECTOR_SESSION_NAME` in
            // zellij-utils/src/input/flock_config.rs — a test keeps them in step.
            session_name "flock-selector"
        }
    }
}
